            <p class="affiliate-note">
              Affiliate link · KASODI may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
            </p>

          </div>

        </div>

      </section>


      <section class="why-we-love">

  <div class="why-we-love-label">
    KASODI NOTE
  </div>

  <div class="why-we-love-content">

    <h2>Why we love it</h2>

    <p>
      This botanical ceramic pitcher has the charm of a vintage find,
      with its softly curved silhouette, delicate floral pattern and
      warm crackle-glaze finish. The ivory, green and ochre palette
      gives it an aged, collected feel without looking overly rustic.
    </p>

    <p>
      At 18 cm tall, it works beautifully as a small flower vase,
      but it is just as lovely styled on its own. We especially like
      it filled with loose garden flowers or placed on a dining table,
      kitchen shelf or console where the botanical detail can become
      part of the room.
    </p>

  </div>

</section>


      <section class="product-care">

  <p class="product-detail-eyebrow">
    CARE
  </p>

  <h2>Keep it looking beautiful</h2>

  <p>
    To help preserve the decorative crackle-glaze finish,
    we recommend gentle hand washing with a soft sponge
    and mild detergent. Avoid abrasive cleaners and sudden
    temperature changes.
  </p>

</section>

      <section class="styling-ideas">

        <div class="styling-heading">
          <p>KASODI STYLING</p>
          <h2>Style it with</h2>
        </div>


       <div class="styling-grid">

  <div class="styling-card">
    <span>01</span>
    <h3>Garden Flowers</h3>
    <p>
      Soft white blooms, muted greenery and delicate seasonal stems
      complement the botanical pattern beautifully.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="styling-card">
    <span>02</span>
    <h3>Natural Linen</h3>
    <p>
      Pair it with ivory, oatmeal or stone-coloured linen to emphasise
      its softly aged, collected character.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="styling-card">
    <span>03</span>
    <h3>Warm Wood</h3>
